.TH "GYRO" "1" "Nov 2026" "Gyro Hosting" "gyro manual"

.SH NAME
gyro-s3-object-lock-set - Set the default retention of a bucket


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgyro s3 object-lock set   [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Set the default retention of a bucket

.PP
Locked buckets only. \fBmode\fR GOVERNANCE or COMPLIANCE with \fBdays\fR 1-3650, or OFF (new objects get no automatic retention; existing locks stay). GOVERNANCE: only Gyro staff can bypass it on request. COMPLIANCE cannot be shortened, switched to GOVERNANCE or removed by anyone (Gyro included) until it expires; the data is kept and the service keeps being billed until then, even after cancellation. Send \fB"confirm": true\fR and \fB"acknowledge": "COMPLIANCE"\fR\&.

.PP
API: PUT /cloud/storage/{id}/buckets/{bucket}/object-lock (operationId setStorageBucketObjectLock, scope services_write)


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--acknowledge\fP=""
	COMPLIANCE only: type COMPLIANCE to accept that it cannot be removed

.PP
\fB--data\fP=""
	request body as JSON, @file or @- (stdin)

.PP
\fB--days\fP=0
	Retention days (not with OFF)

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	show the price quote / request without changing anything

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for set

.PP
\fB--idempotency-key\fP=""
	idempotency key (automatic for money operations)

.PP
\fB--mode\fP=""
	mode (GOVERNANCE|COMPLIANCE|OFF)

.PP
\fB--set\fP=[]
	extra body field key=value (repeatable)


